    <item>
      <title>Understanding Proximity Controllers and RFID Door Access Solutions</title>
      <link>https://mis3085.github.io/docs-chiyu-tech/en/product-categories/proximity-controller-reader/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://mis3085.github.io/docs-chiyu-tech/en/product-categories/proximity-controller-reader/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Proximity Controllers and RFID Door Access: Technology and Solutions 
    &lt;div id=&#34;proximity-controllers-and-rfid-door-access-technology-and-solutions&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    
    &lt;span
        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;
        &lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#proximity-controllers-and-rfid-door-access-technology-and-solutions&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;        
    
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A proximity controller is a universal touchless technology designed to detect nearby objects using electromagnetic fields or beams of electromagnetic radiation, all without physical contact. This technology is widely implemented in RFID door entry systems, which have become an integral part of modern security and access control solutions.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
